<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sakai Tadakatsu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1594–1647</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sakai Tadakatsu was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> from the Sakai family, one of the most trusted hereditary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the Tokugawa. In 1622 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> moved him to Shonai in Dewa province, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> coast, with an assessed yield of about 138,000 koku. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsuruoka">Tsuruoka</a> his castle town, and his descendants ruled Shonai until the end of the domain system.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sakai-tadakatsu.jpg" alt="Sakai Tadakatsu" width="320" height="315" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sakai_Tadakatsu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
